# Spec pipeline

Follow this staged pipeline. Do not skip gates. Do not generate app code before `approval.json` exists with `approved: true`. Do not generate CI/CD.

## Live in this conversation (never delegate)

- New app / gather requirements → follow the `requirements-interview` skill
- Human approval of the five specs → follow the `approve-gate` skill

## Delegate to subagents

1. After `requirements.json` → `architecture-agent`
2. After `architecture.html` + `product-overview.pdf` → `ux-design-agent`
3. After `design-spec.md` → `analytics-agent` and `qa-test-plan-agent` (parallel)
4. After all five specs exist → stop and run `/approve-gate` (live)
5. After `approval.json` → `code-generator-agent` (refuse if unapproved)
6. After scaffold exists → `security-compliance-agent` and `flow-validation-agent` (parallel)
7. After both reports exist → `implementation-agent`

Spec-stage agents produce documents only. Code Generator writes real working code by default; Implementation resolves handoffs and gaps.
